# Ship and fleet events: hardware, physics, distance. One fires on most days.
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

# --- Fleet-wide -------------------------------------------------------------
card storm_shelter
type event
cat grim
days 7 24
weight 7
once
roles A
when cond A ok
when !fired h_flare
text A flare has gone off on the Sun, and its protons will reach the fleet in about forty minutes. {A} packs into the storm shelter between the water tanks with a sleeping bag and a deck of cards, and every crew in the fleet does the same, cards over video, until the dosimeter settles.
do morale A 3
do var storms 1

card storm_shelter2
type event
cat grim
days 25 39
weight 7
once
roles A
when cond A ok
when var storms >= 1
text Another flare, another forty minutes. {A} is in the shelter between the water tanks in six, with the cards already dealt for seven screens. By now everyone knows who cheats at what, and the dosimeter has stopped being the most interesting number in the room.
do morale A 2
do var storms 1

card storm_dose
type event
cat grim
days 11 16
weight 16
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} runs the dosimeter check. Every crew member has now passed fifty millisieverts, more than a nuclear worker in Europe may take in any single year. It was a Tuesday. {A} writes it down and underlines it, and leaves the underline to say the rest.
do trait A curious 1

card comm_delay
type event
cat human
days 16 19
weight 8
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text The signal delay to Earth passes a minute each way. {A} sends a joke to the ground team and waits two and a bit minutes to find out whether it landed. It did, on a slight delay, like everything now.
do morale A 4

card comm_delay2
type event
cat human
due
days 33 38
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Earth is six light-minutes away. {A} asks the ground a yes-or-no question and makes a whole cup of tea before the yes arrives. Conversations have become letters; letters have become weather.
do morale A 1

card earth_dot
type event
cat wonder
days 18 26
weight 5
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} goes to the window to find Earth and has to look for a while. It's a point now, bluish, still one of the brightest things in the sky, and no longer anywhere you could point to a house. {A} photographs it beside the window frame's bolt heads, for scale.
do trait A warm 3

# --- Hardware (controls flavor, never named) ----------------------------------
card scrubber_fault
type event
cat repair
days 2 39
weight 8
once
roles A
when res spares >= 1
text The CO₂ scrubber on {A}'s ship throws its fourth fault since launch. {A} fixes it, then labels it "temperamental" in permanent marker, under a label in Starbase handwriting that already says "be nice to it".
do res spares -1

card boiloff
type event
cat repair skill
days 8 36
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Methane boil-off on {A}'s ship runs high while it flies broadside to feed the solar wings. {A} proposes nose-to-Sun, wings canted, so the ship's own shadow falls down the tanks. The ground runs the power numbers and agrees; boil-off drops by a third, and the attitude goes into everyone's plan.
do res fuel 2
do morale A 2

# --- Hardware (mechanical flavor) --------------------------------------------
# Twin pattern: the tagged copy lets Diego draw this more often; anyone still can.
card tol_stack
type event
cat repair skill
days 6 36
weight 5
once
roles A
when cond A ok
when !fired tol_stack_m
when res spares >= 1
text A replacement pump won't sit in its mount on {A}'s ship. Every part is in tolerance. Stacked together, they're 1.4 millimeters out. {A} shims it with a washer from the spares kit and writes the stack-up on the bulkhead for the next person.
do res spares -1
do morale A 2

card tol_stack_m
type event
cat repair skill
days 6 36
weight 5
once
roles A
when cond A ok
when tag A mech
when !fired tol_stack
when res spares >= 1
text A replacement pump won't sit in its mount on {A}'s ship. Every part is in tolerance. Stacked together, they're 1.4 millimeters out. {A} shims it with a washer from the spares kit and writes the stack-up on the bulkhead for the next person.
do res spares -1
do morale A 2

card hatch_sun
type event
cat repair skill
days 6 38
weight 5
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text The hatch on {A}'s ship sticks whenever the sunward side warms up. {A} works it out on the back of a checklist: the frame grows a millimeter in the sun and the seal doesn't. One new shim, and the door swings the way it did at Starbase.
do morale A 3

# --- Rescue: CO2 scrubber failure -------------------------------------------
card crisis_air
type event
cat repair
once
days 9 36
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
when res spares >= 1
text The CO₂ scrubber on {A}'s ship fails outright. With one person in a cabin that size, the CO₂ only climbs about a twentieth of a percent a day: not an emergency yet, which is the best time to fix one. {A} has the backup running in nine minutes, and it is already complaining.
do morale A -4
do open rescue_air

card rescue_air
type rescue
cat repair
duration 1
roles A B
default send
when apart B A
when cond B ok
text {A}'s ship is breathing on its backup scrubber. It needs a spare cartridge before the backup gives out.
option send | Send a cartridge | A spare cartridge rides the line across in an unscheduled transfer window. {A}'s ship is breathing easy by evening.
  res spares -1
  res fuel -1
  morale A 4
option bring | {B} brings it over | {B} rides the line across with the cartridge in an unscheduled window and stays to help rebuild the primary. By midnight both scrubbers are running, and {B} is asleep on {A}'s floor.
  res spares -1
  res fuel -1
  move B A
  bond A B 10
  morale B 3
